warning: extend_ttl called inside a loop
  --> $DIR/extend_ttl_in_loop.rs:72:9
   |
LL |         env.storage().instance().extend_ttl(TTL_THRESHOLD, TTL_EXTEND_TO); // Should Warn
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = help: each extend_ttl/extend_ttl_with_limits call is a separate metered host call that also writes ledger state, so calling it once per iteration multiplies both costs by the iteration count; batch the extension by collecting the keys/entries first and making a single extension call after the loop (if the entries share one keyed accessor, e.g. multiple keys under Persistent), or extend once with a threshold sized generously enough to cover the whole batch instead of refreshing per-entry per-iteration; the unkeyed Instance::extend_ttl_with_limits form takes threshold arguments rather than a key, so prefer a single generous extension there
   = note: `#[warn(extend_ttl_in_loop)]` on by default

